# Test fixtures: small frozen cases — never re-built by CI
!tests/integration/fixtures/**

# Triple-AI review runtime outputs — per-build artefacts the GitHub
# Action attaches to releases. Curated showcase samples live at
# docs/reviews/ and ARE committed (the negation below).
/reviews/
!docs/reviews/
.claude/

# inSTREAM 7.4 official archive — Cal Poly Humboldt distribution
# (GPL-3.0). Cannot be redistributed under OpenLimno's Apache-2.0;
# users provide their own copy via $OPENLIMNO_INSTREAM7_ARCHIVE or
# ~/.cache/openlimno/instream7_official/. Dev fetch dumps it here.
/output/instream7_official/

# fishtank 教学/课程材料 — 仅本地保留,不纳入公开软件仓库
# (软件必要文件只含 src/tests/examples/pyproject + docs/fishtank/{README,SPEC}.md)
docs/fishtank/slides/
docs/fishtank/notebooks/
docs/fishtank/abm_minicourse/
docs/fishtank/exercises/
docs/fishtank/student_bundle/
docs/fishtank/dist_cli/
docs/fishtank/COURSE_PLAN.md
docs/fishtank/TEACHING_RUNSHEET.md
docs/fishtank/INSTRUCTOR_GUIDE.md
docs/fishtank/CLASS_SIMULATION.md
docs/fishtank/QUICKSTART.md
docs/fishtank/USAGE_WALKTHROUGH.md
docs/fishtank/OPENSOURCE_GUIDE.md
docs/fishtank/CHANGELOG_LOCAL.md
docs/fishtank/REHEARSAL_LOG_*.md

# ...and any archive of that material, wherever it is staged. Every rule above
# is path-specific to docs/fishtank/, so a bundle of exactly those directories
# written anywhere else walks past all of them: on 2026-09-07 a 172 MB
# fishtank_course_materials.zip sat untracked at the repo root, one `git add -A`
# from a commit GitHub would then refuse (100 MB per-file hard limit) and that
# would need history rewriting to undo. ADR-0018's fourth fence is only real if
# it survives the material being packaged. Pinned by
# tests/unit/test_course_material_exclusion.py.
*course_material*
fishtank_course*
student_bundle*
# The patterns above are deliberately broad — material also arrives unpacked,
# as a directory — which means they also match source files merely *named*
# after the thing they exclude. This test is the only such file, and it was in
# fact ignored by its own rule for the length of one `git status`. Negating it
# by name is safer than narrowing the patterns to archive extensions, because
# that would let an unpacked `fishtank_course_materials/` back in.
# test_the_pinning_test_is_not_ignored_by_its_own_rule keeps this honest.
!tests/unit/test_course_material_exclusion.py
